DTEND:20261206T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: H401 WONDER open call: 4-week artist residency 
 in Amsterdam on women in the European Resistance (EUR 3\,000 fee plus prod
 uction budget)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nWomen Narratives during the
  European Resistance (WONDER) is a 15-month EU project (CERV programme) in
  five countries\; each partner hosts one artist\, and this is the Dutch ca
 ll\, for 1 artist.\n\nOrganisation: H401 (Stichting Herengracht 401)\, wit
 hin the EU-funded WONDER project led by ECCOM\nLocation: H401\, Herengrach
 t 401\, Amsterdam\, Netherlands. For artists based in the Netherlands or a
 nother EU member state who can easily travel to Amsterdam\; Dutch proficie
 ncy required.\nAward: Artist fee of EUR 3\,000\, production costs reimburs
 ed up to EUR 1\,000\, plus travel\, accommodation (if applicable) and subs
 istence under EU travel guidelines. Travel and accommodation for the final
  event in Rome are also covered. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 4 w
 eeks between March and April 2027 (can be split into several periods)\, ex
 hibition from the end of April 2027\, final project event in Rome in Decem
 ber 2027\n\nMore: https://h401.org/women-narratives-during-the-european-re
 sistance-wonder/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://h401.org/women-narratives-during-the-european-resistance-wonder
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:H401\, Herengracht 401\, Amsterdam\, Netherlands. For artists base
 d in the Netherlands or another EU member state who can easily travel to A
 msterdam\; Dutch proficiency required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nias-individual-fellowship-2028-29@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261127T165557Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20270315T103000Z
DTEND:20270315T110000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 12:00 CET: NIAS Individual Fellowship 2028-2029 (5 or 10 m
 onths in Amsterdam\; EUR 3\,500 per month stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 15 Mar 2027 at 12:00 CET.\n\nNIAS offers individual fell
 owships to scholars who want to pursue a research project of their own cho
 osing\, working for five or ten months inside an international\, interdisc
 iplinary community of scholars\, writers and artists in the centre of Amst
 erdam.\n\nOrganisation: NIAS-KNAW (Netherlands Institute for Advanced Stud
 y in the Humanities and Social Sciences)\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Netherland
 s. Present at the institute 4 days a week. Open to scholars from the Nethe
 rlands and abroad\; no applications from researchers affiliated with insti
 tutions in Russia or Belarus.\nAward: Personal stipend of EUR 3\,500 per m
 onth\, paid directly to fellows without an affiliation and fellows from ou
 tside the Netherlands. Fellows employed at Dutch universities get a Dutch 
 University Grant of EUR 3\,500 per month paid to the university instead. T
 ravel expenses\, an office and subsidised accommodation are also offered\;
  extra support can be requested by fellows from low-income countries. No a
 pplication fee stated.\nDuration: 5 or 10 months in the academic year 2028
 -2029\n\nMore: https://nias.knaw.nl/fellowships/nias-individual-fellowship
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nias.knaw.nl/fellowships/nias-individual-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands. Present at the institute 4 days a week. O
 pen to scholars from the Netherlands and abroad\; no applications from res
 earchers affiliated with institutions in Russia or Belarus.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:svdj-incubator-2027-jongeren-en-journalistiek@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261127T165557Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270109
SUMMARY:Deadline: SVDJ Incubator 2027: Jongeren en Journalistiek (nine-mont
 h journalism innovation programme\; EUR 20\,000 to 40\,000 participation s
 ubsidy)
DESCRIPTION:The SVDJ Incubator is the Dutch Journalism Fund's innovation pr
 ogramme in which multidisciplinary teams spend nine months researching\, e
 xperimenting and testing around one sector-wide question\; all outcomes ar
 e published open source. The 2027 theme is Jongeren en Journalistiek: how 
 journalism can build durable strategies to strengthen the information posi
 tion of young people aged 16 to 24.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds voo
 r de Journalistiek (SVDJ)\nLocation: Utrecht\, Netherlands (free office sp
 ace near Utrecht Centraal\; mandatory in-person kick-off\, start weekend a
 nd meetings). Programme and call are in Dutch.\nAward: Participation subsi
 dy for the whole programme: EUR 20\,000 at 0.4 fte (16 hours a week)\, EUR
  30\,000 at 0.6 fte (24 hours) or EUR 40\,000 at 0.8 fte (32 hours). Plus 
 a travel allowance of EUR 0 to 400 a month depending on distance to Utrech
 t (up to EUR 3\,600 in total)\; the page lists the application amount as E
 UR 20\,000 to 43\,600. A further EUR 400\,000 pot is available to teams du
 ring the programme for short projects and experiments. If you are seconded
  by an employer\, the employer receives the subsidy.\nDuration: Nine month
 s\, 2 March to 30 November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.svdj.nl/regeling/svdj
 -incubator/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.svdj.nl/regeling/svdj-incubator/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Utrecht\, Netherlands (free office space near Utrecht Centraal\; m
 andatory in-person kick-off\, start weekend and meetings). Programme and c
 all are in Dutch.
END:VEVENT
